@tradition wall-night
// W3 rec deck words. Tuesdays 18:30-19:45 from Day 2, the climbing wall; Tomas belays. Climb and ring the bell; your name on the season's bell board in the foyer.
== mail
- Wall night tomorrow, {time} at the climbing wall. Tomas will belay. Climb any route, ring the bell at the top, and your name goes on the season's bell board in the foyer.
== ask
- Wall night tonight! Tomas is belaying. He's very careful. Slightly too careful.   #funny
- Come and ring the bell later. Everyone cheers. Even for me.
- Climbing tonight. Red, yellow, blue or green. Pick one and go up.
== here
- Climb on! You've got it.
- Ding! Another one on the bell board.
- Feet first, then hands. Always feet.
== thanks
- You clip into a belay at the foot of the wall. Tomas gives you a thumbs up. The bell's a long way up.
== chatter
- My arms are dead. I rang the bell, though.   #funny
- The season's bell board's filling up. Has your name gone on yet?
- Vance has rung that bell more than anyone. He has a number. He'll tell you.   #funny
